{"id":3772,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/adjectives/","parentId":540,"order":40,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Adjectives: Old, interesting, expensive, etc.","seo":{"title":"Adjectives: Old, interesting, expensive, etc. - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use adjectives in this A1 Elementary grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1%E2%80%93Grammar_adjectives.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T09:22:18","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms with adjectives to complete the following sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"427\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Put the words in the correct order.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"428\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the senteces using <em>(a/an)</em> adjective + noun or using <em>be</em> + adjective.</h5> <p><em>EXAMPLE: heavy / table ⇒ This table <span class=\"textGap\">is heavy</span> . It’s <span class=\"textGap\">a heavy table</span>.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"429\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Adjectives in English – grammar chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-10929\" src=\"/media/uploads/adjectives-english.png\" alt=\"Colorful educational chart explaining the use of adjectives in English grammar with examples in sentences, showing adjective-noun combinations, the use of adjectives with 'am/is/are', sensory verbs, and the rule against pluralizing adjectives.\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4>Adjective + noun</h4> <p>When we use adjectives with a noun in English, the adjectives go <strong>before the noun</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>It’s an <span><strong>expensive guitar</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>It’s a <span><strong>guitar </strong><strong>expensive</strong></span>.&nbsp;<span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> <li><em>She has a <span><strong>new car</strong></span>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She has a <span><strong>car </strong><strong>new</strong></span>. <span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Am/is/are</strong> + adjective</h4> <p>We can also use adjectives without a noun after the verb&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple-forms-of-to-be/\">be</a></strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>This guitar <span><strong>is expensive</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>Her car <span><strong>is new</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>In questions, the adjective can go after <strong>be</strong> + subject.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Is your car <span><strong>new</strong></span>?&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>Are your classmates <span><strong>nice</strong></span>?&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Feel/look/smell/sound/taste</strong> + adjective</h4> <p>We can also use adjectives without a noun after the <a href=\"/grammar-points/b1-b2/verbs-of-the-senses/\">verbs of the senses</a>:&nbsp;<strong>feel, look, smell, sound,&nbsp;</strong><strong>taste</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Your idea <span><strong>sounds interesting</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I don’t like this soup. It <span><strong>tastes horrible</strong></span>.</em></li> <li><em>You <span><strong>look tired</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>These cookies <span><strong>smell delicious</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I<span><strong> feel depressed</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <h4>No plural</h4> <p>Adjectives in English have <strong>no plural</strong>. They are always singular.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>These are my&nbsp;<span><strong>favourite</strong></span> shoes. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>These are my&nbsp;<span><strong>favourites</strong></span>&nbsp;shoes.</em> <em><span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> <li><em>She has <span><strong>blue</strong></span> eyes. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>She has <span><strong>blues</strong></span> eyes. <span><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></span></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>Very/quite</strong></h4> <p>We can use <strong>very</strong> and <strong>quite</strong> before the adjectives.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>It’s <span><strong>very</strong></span> expensive.</em></li> <li><em>It’s <span><strong>quite</strong></span> expensive</em>.</li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":427,"questions":[{"id":3696,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>With this makeup, your eyes <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["look different","different look","look differents"]}]},{"id":3697,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These are <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["important documents","documents importants","documents important"]}]},{"id":3698,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p><span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in their new house?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Are happy they","Are they happy","Are they happies"]}]},{"id":3699,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>He has <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["a job interesting","an interesting job"]}]},{"id":3700,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sit down. You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["look tired","tired look","smell tired"]}]},{"id":3701,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Our holidays <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["fantastic are","are fantastic","are fantastics"]}]},{"id":3702,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>John has problems at home. <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["Are goods his marks","Are his marks good","Are good his marks"]}]},{"id":3703,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Their project <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["interesting looks","tastes interesting","sounds interesting"]}]},{"id":3704,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>These cookies <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["are excellent","are excellents","excellent are"]}]},{"id":3705,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Her eyes <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["blue are","are blues","are blue"]}]}]},{"id":428,"questions":[{"id":3706,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Which is the correct order? </div>","choices":[{"id":7910,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>Your great idea is.</span>"},{"id":7911,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>Your idea is great.</span>"},{"id":7912,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>Great your idea is.</span>"},{"id":7913,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>Your idea great is.</span>"}]},{"id":3707,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>Which is the correct order? </div>","choices":[{"id":7914,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>She an exceptional student is.</span>"},{"id":7915,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>She is a student exceptional.</span>"},{"id":7916,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>She is an exceptional student.</span>"},{"id":7917,"letter":"D.","html":"<span>She 